---
description: Writing style for Markdown documentation
globs: "**/*.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use short, direct sentences in the active voice.
- Explain how a thing works and why, not only what it is.
- Define each term once, in `GLOSSARY.md` when the project has one, and use it with one meaning.
- Give each heading a name that says what the section contains, and keep one idea per paragraph.
- Prefer a concrete example over an abstract description. Keep code examples complete enough to run.
- Leave out promotional words such as "powerful", "seamless", "robust" or "cutting-edge", and leave out emojis.
- Remove sentences that do not change what the reader knows or does.
